{
	title: 'Opt-in web scroll probe',
	spec: 'config.ason scrollDebug (boolean, default false, listed by /config, sent to the page) turns on a web transcript scroll probe (src/web/scroll-debug.ts). It finds what moves the reading position. While on, the page records: every write to the transcript scroll position (scrollTop, scrollTo, scrollBy, scrollIntoView inside it) and window.scrollTo, with the first stack frames; the named code path that asked for it (scroll.note: bottom, land, prepend, follow, settled, restore, settle, shift, showEnd, end, top, switch, page, reveal); scroll events (one per 100 ms); SHIFT when the row at the view center moves over 2px in the content; JUMP when the view moves over a screen with no finger down, with ms since the last caught write (large: the browser moved it); touch, lift, focus and visibility. Each row holds scrollTop, scrollHeight, clientHeight, the space above the rows, the first mounted row key and the center row key and offset; no text. The log keeps 5000 rows in localStorage (hal.scrollLog), so it survives an iOS reload. /scroll-log (needs the setting) sends a scroll-log event to every web socket; each page posts its log in batches of 100 rows to POST /scroll-debug (logged-in, same-origin, only while the setting is on, under 4 MB), and the host appends one JSON line per row to state/scroll-debug.log, rotating like composer-debug.log. A timebomb test in src/host/web-diagnostics.test.ts fails on 2026-12-15 and says what to delete.',
	status: 'done',
	needs: ['s37']
}
